-- A landlord gives notice, and later seeks possession, which needs the notice.
-- The two are the sides of a RAND, with the side that makes the record (the
-- notice) on the left. The sides take the trace's events in step, so the read
-- at 400 sees the notice recorded at 10: this file runs, and so does
-- reader-first.l4, the same file with the sides swapped.
-- (smucclaw/l4-ide#1069)

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Landlord
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF `gives notice`, `seeks possession`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`notice` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `gives notice`
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `notice given` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`possession` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord
    MAY `seeks possession` PROVIDED (RECALL OFFICIAL's `notice given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WITHIN 1000
    HENCE COMMIT `possession sought` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the tenancy` MEANS `notice` RAND `possession`

#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Landlord DOES `gives notice` AT 10
    PARTY Landlord DOES `seeks possession` AT 400
